    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36185" root="قمح" body-key="q">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قُمَاحٌ</span></b> , a subst. from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَمَحَ</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَامَحَ</span>, <i>Aversion</i> of
a camel <i>from drinking, by reason of the thirst's
being satisfied,</i> or <i>of loathing,</i> or <i>of the coldness
of the water,</i> or <i>of some disease.</i> (L. [See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُمَامٌ</span>.]) Hence <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَهْرَا قُمَاحٍ</span>, also called <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَهْرَا</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قِمَاحٍ</span>: see 3.

